  "description": "LIRREM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C140 H144 Gd4 N12 O16,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.573-3.886 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.33-112.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ3-OH)2(tmhd)4L6]·2CH3CN (C144H150Gd4N14O16). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
